y","desc":"Expected goals for per 60 on the power play.","lower":false,"fmt":"2","kind":"team","stabilises_at":null},{"key":"pk","label":"Penalty kill","desc":"Expected goals against per 60 short-handed.","lower":true,"fmt":"2","kind":"team","stabilises_at":null},{"key":"goalie","label":"Goaltending","desc":"Team goals saved above expected per 60.","lower":false,"fmt":"2","kind":"team","stabilises_at":null},{"key":"xgf_pct5","label":"5v5 xGF%","desc":"Share of 5v5 expected goals.","lower":false,"fmt":"2","kind":"team","stabilises_at":null},{"key":"cf_pct5","label":"5v5 CF%","desc":"Share of 5v5 shot attempts.","lower":false,"fmt":"2","kind":"team","stabilises_at":null}]}],"model":[{"key":"xg","label":"Expected goals (xG)","group":"Shots","desc":"The probability that an unblocked attempt becomes a goal (LightGBM) from distance, angle, shot type, rebound (time and angle change since the previous attempt), rush (time since a neutral- or defensive-zone event), time since and type and location of the previous event, strength, score state and an arena adjustment for scorer bias (seasons before 2023-24); cross-fitted by season so no shot is scored by a model that saw it; benchmarked against MoneyPuck's xGoal (credit: xG benchmark data from MoneyPuck.com). When the model does not score a season the build uses a logistic fallback fitted on the season's own attempts and says so (xg_source)."},{"key":"shooting","label":"Shooting talent","group":"Shots","desc":"Goals above expected per unblocked attempt, regressed toward the league by the stabilisation constant of finishing (most of a season's goals-above-xG is noise)."},{"key":"goalies","label":"GSAx","group":"Goaltending","desc":"Goals saved above expected: the xG of the unblocked attempts a goalie faces minus the goals he allows, overall, by danger band (xG under 0.08, 0.08-0.20, 0.20+), by shot type and by strength; empty-net goals excluded."},{"key":"onice","label":"On-ice rates","group":"Skaters","desc":"Shot attempts, unblocked attempts, shots, goals and xG for and against per 60 with the player on the ice at 5v5, on the power play and short-handed; the adjusted versions are score- and venue-adjusted (each event weighted by how its score state and venue inflate or deflate rates league-wide)."},{"key":"rapm","label":"RAPM","group":"Skaters","desc":"Regularised adjusted plus-minus: a ridge regression on 5v5 stints where every skater has an offence and a defence coefficient, with team-mates, opponents, zone starts, score state and home ice controlled, and priors from earlier seasons; the coefficients are isolated xG for and against per 60."},{"key":"value","label":"Rink value","group":"Value","desc":"Goals above replacement (GAR) and wins (WAR): RAPM offence and defence, power play and penalty kill, shooting talent, penalties drawn and taken and faceoffs, in goals over a replacement-level player (the level of the players outside each team's regular lineup); goalies from GSAx against replacement goaltending."},{"key":"lines","label":"Lines","group":"Skaters","desc":"Forward trios and defence pairs from the shift charts: every 5v5 stint with three forwards and two defencemen on a side counts toward that line and that pair."},{"key":"team_strength","label":"Team strength","group":"Teams","desc":"Score- and venue-adjusted xG and shot rates by strength, special teams, a goaltending component with the expected starter as an input, and schedule effects (rest, travel, back-to-backs)."},{"key":"game","label":"Game model","group":"Prediction","desc":"Goals for each side from the team-strength components, starters and context, with correlation, empty-net and late-game effects; outputs the win probability, regulation result, overtime and shootout probabilities, puck line and total."},{"key":"live","label":"Win probability","group":"Prediction","desc":"A Markov model of the remaining goals at every event from score, time, strength and the pre-game expectation; without it the page uses a Poisson model of the remaining goals at the pre-game rates (labelled)."},{"key":"season_sim","label":"Season simulation","group":"Prediction","desc":"The remaining schedule simulated game by game (84 games from 2026-27), points (win 2, OT / SO loss 1), the NHL tiebreak procedure, divisional and wild-card seeding, best-of-seven series, the Presidents' Trophy and the draft lottery; magic numbers and next-game odds."},{"key":"awards","label":"Award races","group":"Prediction","desc":"Hart, Vezina, Norris, Calder, Art Ross, Maurice Richard and Selke probabilities from the projected season and a fit on verified past winners."},{"key":"percentile","label":"Percentiles","group":"Catalogue","desc":"100 = best, reversed where lower is better; placed against the qualified pool (skaters: 250 minutes at 5v5 per 82 team games, prorated; goalies: a quarter of the team's minutes) after shrinking the value toward the pool mean with the metric's stabilisation constant: (n v + k m) / (n + k); a metric needs its sample floor (50 minutes at 5v5, 20 shots, 50 faceoffs, 20 PP or PK minutes, 100 unblocked attempts faced) before it gets a percentile. pct_pos compares forwards with forwards and defencemen with defencemen."},{"key":"stabilisation","label":"Stabilisation","group":"Catalogue","desc":"The sample at which split-half reliability reaches 0.7: r(n) = n / (n + k), n_0.7 = 0.7 k / 0.3 (k fitted per metric over seasons)."},{"key":"strength","label":"Strength states","group":"Catalogue","desc":"5v5: five skaters a side with both goalies in net; PP / SH: the player's team has more / fewer skaters; other: 4v4, 3v3, empty net. Regular-season shootouts are excluded from every count."},{"key":"game_score","label":"Game score","group":"Games","desc":"Three stars: 0.75 G + 0.7 A1 + 0.55 A2 + 0.075 SOG + 0.05 BLK + 0.15 penalties drawn - 0.15 taken + 0.01 FOW - 0.01 FOL + 0.05 CF - 0.05 CA + 0.15 GF - 0.15 GA (5v5 on-ice terms); goalies -0.75 GA + 0.1 saves."}],"notices":{"moneypuck":"xG benchmark data from MoneyPuck.com","nhl":"NHL data shown for informational, non-commercial use; no affiliation with the NHL, NHLPA, teams, players, ESPN or bookmakers."}}